# Bridge runtime state. The real watch root lives at ~/macrovoice (or, on an
# install that predates the rename, ~/mw-bridge), outside the repo. These rules
# only catch a watch root someone pointed INTO the repo by mistake.
#
# DO NOT "finish the rename" by adding /macrovoice/ here. That is the Python
# package directory. Ignoring it would make every new module in the package
# invisible to `git add`, on a repo whose .gitignore already fails closed and
# where `git status` is therefore not a reliable alarm. Pinned by
# tests/test_watch.py.
/mw-bridge/
.spool/
.staging/
.drain.lock
.last-publish
*.log
/watch/
/scratch/
**/tmp/

# Local working material. This repo is developed alongside a research workspace
# and a generated code graph, both of which sit in the same folder and are not
# part of the published tool. They are kept out of git rather than out of the
# directory, so the working tree stays usable while the repo stays just the tool.
docs/
evidence/
upstream/
graphify-out/
.graphifyignore

# Agent working state: task briefs, plans and review diffs written by the superpowers
# skills. Same category as docs/: a record of how the work was done, not part of the tool.
# Listed here on 2026-08-11 so it fails closed like everything else. It was already ignored
# in practice, but only by a nested `.superpowers/sdd/.gitignore` containing `*`, which is
# written by the skill and could vanish with a skill update or a re-scaffold. The `.md` files
# under it would still be caught by the `*.md` rule below; the review `.diff` files would not
# have been, so the protection rested on a file this repo does not control.
.superpowers/

# Markdown is private by default.
#
# Notes, working docs and captured output live in this folder next to the code.
# Listing each one by name meant a new note was tracked until someone remembered
# to add it, which is the wrong way round for files that are not meant to ship.
# This fails closed instead: a new .md is ignored unless it is named below.
*.md

# The un-ignored set: conventional public-facing repo docs. Declared up front,
# even though most do not exist yet, so that creating one later does not silently
# produce an untracked file. Root-anchored, so a note that happens to share one of
# these names deeper in the tree stays ignored.
!/README.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE.md
# LICENSE with no extension is not matched by *.md and needs no rule.

# GitHub's own markdown surfaces: issue and PR templates, funding notes. Safe as a
# glob because .github/ is not itself excluded; a negation cannot resurrect a file
# inside an excluded directory, which is why the directory rules above are absolute.
!/.github/**/*.md
